00:32:10,061 --> 00:32:15,920
the idea of using magnets as repositories for information.

385
00:32:15,921 --> 00:32:19,440
A north pole up gives one measure of something.

386
00:32:19,860 --> 00:32:22,660
A north pole down gives another measure of things.

387
00:32:22,661 --> 00:32:26,800
And once we can say this is yes and this is no,

388
00:32:27,160 --> 00:32:29,500
then we can build a memory device out of it.

389
00:32:30,660 --> 00:32:33,500
Most computers today come equipped with hard drives

390
00:32:33,501 --> 00:32:35,780
featuring a layer embedded with tiny magnets.

391
00:32:37,320 --> 00:32:39,880
The north-south configurations of those magnets

392
00:32:39,881 --> 00:32:41,320
contain encoded information.

393
00:32:42,460 --> 00:32:45,540
The hard drive is magnetic.

394
00:32:45,920 --> 00:32:54,260
There is a read-write head in the computer that rides just above this rotating disk,

395
00:32:54,261 --> 00:33:02,260
and as it rotates, it writes and reads little bits and bytes of information on that disk.

396
00:33:02,800 --> 00:33:06,420
It could be a south pole, and next to it, it might write a north pole,

397
00:33:06,540 --> 00:33:08,840
so you'd have a one and a zero.

398
00:33:10,380 --> 00:33:14,420
Ones and zeros are the components of the so-called binary language of computers.

399
00:33:15,920 --> 00:33:19,420
What would appear to us as an ocean of indecipherable numbers

400
00:33:19,421 --> 00:33:22,920
contains data easily digestible by the computer's processor.

401
00:33:24,920 --> 00:33:28,920
Magnetic hard drives, however, retain only part of a computer's data.

402
00:33:30,420 --> 00:33:32,920
Semiconductors provide its primary memory,

403
00:33:32,921 --> 00:33:35,420
in which most of the computing takes place.

404
00:33:36,920 --> 00:33:40,920
The semiconductor memory known as RAM is faster,

405
00:33:40,921 --> 00:33:43,420
but carries a distinct disadvantage.

406
00:33:43,421 --> 00:33:47,420
When you shut off the power, the data disappear.

407
00:33:49,420 --> 00:33:55,420
