00:34:22,300 --> 00:34:24,440
And so when you turn the computer back on,

414
00:34:24,680 --> 00:34:28,060
all the information is still there and the computer comes on immediately

415
00:34:28,061 --> 00:34:30,620
without having to wait for it to boot up.

416
00:34:31,880 --> 00:34:35,800
To determine which magnetic material might make the best MRAM chip,

417
00:34:35,801 --> 00:34:40,800
Researchers place samples in a machine called an alternating gradient magnetometer.

